@format 1
@id section-naming.switch-inline-edit-target
@title Switch inline rename target
@section Section naming
@area In Split tab
@entry other-row-double-click
@summary Show how a normal double-click on a different section first commits the currently edited row on the first click's mouse-up, then opens the replacement inline editor on the second click.
@related section-naming.inline-editor-open, section-naming.inline-editor-input
@tag section
@tag split
@tag naming
@tag renaming
@tag inline-editor

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[other-row-double-click] Different section row double-clicked <input>
= A different section row receives a normal double-click while pSectionIndexEditing still identifies the old row and its inline fields may contain uncommitted text.
> first-click-press

[first-click-press] First click establishes released row <process>
- The first PreviewMouseLeftButtonDown records the clicked row as pSectionRowDragging and captures the row panel; while inline editing is active PSectionMoveHandle does not start a drag @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...)
  @ panel.PSectionMoveHandle(...)
> first-click-release

[first-click-release] First click mouse-up resolves different row <process>
- PSectionUpHandle releases capture, resolves the clicked row index, and because it differs from pSectionIndexEditing enters the commit-and-select path @ panel.PSectionUpHandle(...)
> commit-old

[commit-old] Commit current inline editor <process>
- PSectionEditCommit trims the old row's current name/prefix/suffix fields, clears the tracked editor references, sends the values to PFlowNameSet, and rebuilds the section panel @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
  @ flow.PFlowNameSet(...)
> select-new-row

[select-new-row] Select row from first click <process>
- After the old editor commit returns, PSectionUpHandle selects the clicked row through PFlowSectionSelect @ panel.PSectionUpHandle(...)
  @ flow.PFlowSectionSelect(...)
> second-click

[second-click] Second click opens rename path <process>
- The second MouseLeftButtonDown has ClickCount at least two, so the row handler releases capture/drag state, resolves and selects that row, assigns pSectionIndexEditing to it, and rebuilds the panel @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...)
  @ flow.PFlowSectionSelect(...)
> build-new-editor

[build-new-editor] Build replacement inline fields <process>
- During the rebuild, PSectionEditorBuild creates and tracks name/prefix/suffix TextBoxes initialized from the newly selected row's stored LPiece values @ panel.PSectionEditorBuild(...)
> rebuild-focus-loss

[rebuild-focus-loss] Rebuild-time LostFocus does not queue old close <process>
- LostFocus raised while PSectionRebuild is actively replacing controls reaches PSectionEditClose, which returns immediately while pSectionRebuilding is true instead of scheduling a deferred commit against replacement editor references @ panel.PSectionEditClose(...)
> switched

[switched] Inline rename target switched <output>
= The previous row's buffered text has been committed before the replacement editor opens, and the new inline editor now represents the double-clicked row.
